 and  requirements and their pay ranges  between a minimum of 7 to 8 lakhs per  annum to a maximum of 40 to 50 lakhs per  annum  service based companies are majorly mass  recruiters and they are pay ranges  between a minimum of 2 to 3 lakhs per  annum to a maximum of 12 lakhs per annum  the second category is non-technical  companies which are not related to  technology and primarily focus on  business for example companies like kpmp  white ice etc hire consulting or  management profiles where your major  responsibility is interacting with the  client this type of profile primarily  requires good communication skills which  help you interact with people and build  a positive personality if you are a  person who is good at communication  skills and presentation skills you can  go for the non-technical companies  the last category is core companies  these companies are highly specialized  in their core industries and are highly  rated for their skills and experience  these companies offer jobs in the core  areas of engineering such as mechanical  civil electrical etc for example the  tata industry's most successful and  biggest business unit in india hires  most mechanical engineering students and  other companies such as avcon's  infrastructure limited and punch lloyd  hire several brand students which  majorly focuses on construction  the second sector you can build your  career in is the government sector the  government sector is also called the  public sector which includes the public  goods and governmental services such as  the military law enforcement and many  more some students want to work in the  government sector after their btec or be  for which they will prepare from the  second or third year of engineering if  you are interested in doing online jobs  after your graduation you can take up  the following government exams  upsc union public service commission is  the most popular and known by everyone  and as a recruiting agency for top-level  central government jobs such as ias ips  etc the next is ssc cgl staff selection  commission combined graduate level  this exam will help you become an  inspector sub-inspector etc the next are  some of the public sector banks ibps sbi  if you are interested in working in a  bank you can take up some ibps and other  bank exams like sbi etc if you are  interested in developing or innovating  and in research you can become a  scientist and esro or drdo  the last sector is psus psus is the  public sector undertakings these are the  companies where the 51 share is of the  government and 49 share is of private  companies here you will get the benefits  of both government and private companies  in india you have so many psus in  different categories like transportation  banking hospital insurance etc some of  the psus are bharat petroleum indian oil  corporation esro bsnl bhel sale ntpc  dmrs etc you can visit their website to  see the requirements and eligibility and  apply for your interested one if you are  interested in higher studies you can  offer masters in ms m-tech and me for ms  you can prepare for exams like gre and  t-o-e-f-l or toffel  if you are interested in mtech you can  prepare for exams like gate jntu cet if  you want to go for me you can prepare  for exams like gate t-a-n-c-e-t  try applying for a teaching position for  btec be or bca students if you don't  have strong coding skills but are a  master in theoretical concepts  so till now you got to know the  different career options after  completing your btec i hope you guys  like this video do share this with your  friends and let me know your career  option after btec in the comment box for  more updates visit our simply learn  youtube channel thanks for watching stay  safe and keep learning  hi there if you like this video  subscribe to the simply learn youtube  channel and click here to watch similar  videos turn it up and get certified  click here
 

